{"case_id":"T8051","gap_exists":false,"gap_type":[],"confidence":94,"affected_functions":["ares_u32_from_ptr","ares_rc4_generate_key"],"reason":"The change only alters entropy mixing in the internal RC4 fallback seed path, replacing bitwise OR with XOR for pointer and time-derived values. No fuzz-controlled bytes, parser semantics, API protocol, or state transition reach these expressions. Under FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION, ares_rc4_generate_key instead executes srand(0), bypassing every changed time/pointer-mixing expression. H0 therefore does not cover the modified logic, but the missing coverage is not a material fuzz-harness gap because the behavior is environment-derived rather than input-driven.","evidence":["H0 sends data only through ares_dns_parse, DNS record accessors, and ares_dns_write.","ares_u32_from_ptr consumes only an address and changes its two pointer halves from OR to XOR.","ares_rc4_generate_key derives data from rc4_state, &i, and ares_tvnow(&tv), not from a fuzz input.","The FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION branch calls srand(0) and excludes the changed pointer/time seed calculations.","ares_rc4_generate_key accepts only rc4_state, key, and key_len, with key_len required to equal ARES_RC4_KEY_LEN; the changed expressions introduce no variable-format input parser or protocol."],"recommended_action":"Do not add a fuzz target for this change. If validation is desired, use focused deterministic or statistical tests for ares_u32_from_ptr and the non-fuzzing fallback seed construction, since H0's parser-oriented fuzzing and the fuzz-build configuration cannot meaningfully evaluate entropy mixing."}
